In article <1992Feb18.220945.1379@cs.wayne.edu>, dfl@math.wayne.edu (David Frohardt-Lane) writes:
> Is there any way (besides a scroll of identify) of telling whether you
> have the Amulet of Yendor or an imitation?

The only REAL amulet you'll ever get is the one on the level where the Wizard
of Yendor is guarding it. Any others you come across, eg guarded by demons in
maze levels, or by wishing, or by (blessed) create monster, are cheap plastic
imitations.

Once you have the real amulet, the Wizard may occasionally steal it from you;
when you kill him, you may find an extra one and have to waste a scroll of
identify on it. The easy way to get round this is to name the real one as soon
as you get it - this method shouldn't work, but it does, and is very useful!

Marius
